          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "జేబుదొంగ — jēbudoṅga — \"a pickpocket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రద్దీ బస్సులో జేబుదొంగ నా పర్సు కొట్టేశాడు. raddī bassulō jēbudoṅga nā parsu koṭṭēśāḍu. In the crowded bus a pickpocket took my purse."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "జేబు, a pocket, + దొంగ, a thief."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "జేబుదొంగ (jēbudoṅga) is a Telugu compound: జేబు, \"a pocket\", a loan from Arabic jayb through Persian and Hindustani, and దొంగ, \"a thief\", native Dravidian (DEDR 2982)."
            }
          ]
        },
